  "2026-08-28T08:13:08.155Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: searched all statuses for GH-1135, GH-1040, GH-1004, GH-976, item_hash_version, writer-version repair loops, and changed=false byte rewrites; fully read closed pm-0wfdim, pm-igdvfq, and pm-2htk4p. Those owners implemented epoch-aware verification and repair, while #1135 is a fresh post-fix three-repository reproduction that names same-version-marker hash divergence and a false repair receipt. This open unclaimed recurrence is canonical for GitHub #1135."
  "2026-08-28T08:13:51.701Z","harness:codex","GitHub linkage evidence: #1135 comment https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1135#issuecomment-5450113598 points to this canonical PM item and its merge-stable main-branch .toon path."
  "2026-08-28T23:24:18.291Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: focused history and recovery suites passed; live pm validate checked 2,596 items with zero history drift and zero version skew in the current workspace; full repository coverage passed 8,099 tests at exact 100/100/100/100."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T23:24:36.998Z","harness:codex","Persisted hash algorithms are format capabilities, not implementation details. Any hash-input change must advance the writer epoch so readers can classify skew separately from corruption."
